From: NixOS maintainers <maintainers@nixos.org>
Subject: [PATCH] tools: compiler: match glibc 2.42 __attribute_const__ definition exactly

glibc 2.42 defines __attribute_const__ as:
    # define __attribute_const__ __attribute__ ((__const__))
in sys/cdefs.h (note the space before the first parenthesis).

The kernel tools header previously defined it as empty.  GCC 15 warns
when a macro is redefined to a different replacement list, and that
warning is treated as -Werror in resolve_btfids and other host tools.

Change the kernel tools definition to the exact token sequence glibc
uses, including the space before "((".  With identical replacement lists
the preprocessor accepts the redefinition silently per C11 6.10.3.

--- a/tools/include/linux/compiler.h
+++ b/tools/include/linux/compiler.h
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@
 
 #ifndef __attribute_const__
-# define __attribute_const__
+# define __attribute_const__ __attribute__ ((__const__))
 #endif
 
 #ifndef __maybe_unused
